# Wave H.a — Platform Tour Ops API base

## Path choice

Hostile audit / remaining thin-shell checklist: `apps/web/src/urban/` still hosts **platform** BFF egress (`resolveTourOpsApiBaseUrl`) used by ~80 admin server/BFF files. That makes the shell look like an Urban product host when the helper is product-blind (re-export of `@app-cloud/guest-surface-host`).

Wave H continues admin product-dir shrinkage. This tranche is the highest fan-in cut with lowest product-risk.

## Decision

1. Move SoT to `apps/web/src/platform/tour-ops-api-base.ts`:
   - `resolveTourOpsApiBaseUrl` / `assertGuestBffProductionConfig` from guest-surface-host
   - `buildPublicTenantHeaders(tenantId)` (neutral name)
   - Compat aliases removed (Gap Closure B.12); use `buildPublicTenantHeaders` / `resolveTourOpsApiBaseUrl`
2. Retarget all `@/urban/urban-api-base` (and relative) imports to `@/platform/tour-ops-api-base`.
3. **Delete** `apps/web/src/urban/urban-api-base.ts` (no shim).
4. Update PSC parity / catalog access specs to the new path.

## Out of scope (later H)

- Delete remaining `src/urban/*` (catalog client, settings panel, settings route)
- Delete `src/denali/denali-catalog-client.ts`
- Shrink `wizard/denali/` host adapters
- Brand fallback mark kind `"denali"` / IgnorePlugin env gates

## Verify

```bash
test ! -f apps/web/src/urban/urban-api-base.ts
rg '@/urban/urban-api-base|urban/urban-api-base' apps/web
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/guest-api-base-parity.spec.ts \
  test/guest-bff-env.spec.ts \
  test/urban-catalog-access.spec.ts \
  test/workspace-boundary.spec.ts
```
